#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:1
msgid "Release 2.19 (2023-11-17)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:3
msgid ""
"The experimental `nix` command can now act as a [shebang interpreter](../"
"command-ref/new-cli/nix.md#shebang-interpreter) by appending the contents of "
"any `#! nix` lines and the script's location into a single call."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:6
msgid ""
"[URL flake references](../command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md#flake-"
"references) now support [percent-encoded](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/"
"html/rfc3986#section-2.1) characters."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:8
msgid ""
"[Path-like flake references](../command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md#path-like-"
"syntax) now accept arbitrary unicode characters (except `#` and `?`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:10
msgid ""
"The experimental feature `repl-flake` is no longer needed, as its "
"functionality is now part of the `flakes` experimental feature. To get the "
"previous behavior, use the `--file/--expr` flags accordingly."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:12
msgid ""
"There is a new flake installable syntax `flakeref#.attrPath` where the \".\" "
"prefix specifies that `attrPath` is interpreted from the root of the flake "
"outputs, with no searching of default attribute prefixes like `packages."
"<SYSTEM>` or `legacyPackages.<SYSTEM>`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:14
msgid ""
"Nix adds `apple-virt` to the default system features on macOS systems that "
"support virtualization. This is similar to what's done for the `kvm` system "
"feature on Linux hosts."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:16
msgid ""
"Add a new built-in function [`builtins.convertHash`](../language/builtins."
"md#builtins-convertHash)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:18
msgid "`nix-shell` shebang lines now support single-quoted arguments."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:20
msgid ""
"`builtins.fetchTree` is now its own experimental feature, [`fetch-tree`](../"
"development/experimental-features.md#xp-feature-fetch-tree). This allows "
"stabilising it independently of the rest of what is encompassed by [`flakes`]"
"(../development/experimental-features.md#xp-feature-flakes)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:23
msgid "The interface for creating and updating lock files has been overhauled:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:25
msgid ""
"[`nix flake lock`](../command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-lock.md) only creates "
"lock files and adds missing inputs now. It will _never_ update existing "
"inputs."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:28
msgid ""
"[`nix flake update`](../command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-update.md) does the "
"same, but _will_ update inputs."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:29
msgid ""
"Passing no arguments will update all inputs of the current flake, just like "
"it already did."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:30
msgid ""
"Passing input names as arguments will ensure only those are updated. This "
"replaces the functionality of `nix flake lock --update-input`"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:31
msgid ""
"To operate on a flake outside the current directory, you must now pass `--"
"flake path/to/flake`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:33
msgid ""
"The flake-specific flags `--recreate-lock-file` and `--update-input` have "
"been removed from all commands operating on installables. They are "
"superseded by `nix flake update`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:36
msgid ""
"Commit signature verification for the [`builtins.fetchGit`](../language/"
"builtins.md#builtins-fetchGit) is added as the new [`verified-fetches` "
"experimental feature](../development/experimental-features.md#xp-feature-"
"verified-fetches)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:38
msgid ""
"[`nix path-info --json`](../command-ref/new-cli/nix3-path-info.md) "
"(experimental) now returns a JSON map rather than JSON list. The `path` "
"field of each object has instead become the key in the outer map, since it "
"is unique. The `valid` field also goes away because we just use `null` "
"instead."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:43
msgid "Old way:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:45
msgid ""
"```json5\n"
"[\n"
"  {\n"
"    \"path\": \"/nix/store/fvqsvk65d38p8qqir371ii0hyqxvjcw6-bash-5.2-p15\",\n"
"    \"valid\": true,\n"
"    // ...\n"
"  },\n"
"  {\n"
"    \"path\": \"/nix/store/wffw7l0alvs3iw94cbgi1gmmbmw99sqb-home-manager-"
"path\",\n"
"    \"valid\": false\n"
"  }\n"
"]\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:59
msgid "New way"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:61
msgid ""
"```json5\n"
"{\n"
"  \"/nix/store/fvqsvk65d38p8qqir371ii0hyqxvjcw6-bash-5.2-p15\": {\n"
"    // ...\n"
"  },\n"
"  \"/nix/store/wffw7l0alvs3iw94cbgi1gmmbmw99sqb-home-manager-path\": null,\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:70
msgid ""
"This makes it match `nix derivation show`, which also maps store paths to "
"information."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:72
msgid ""
"When Nix is installed using the [binary installer](../installation/"
"installing-binary.md), in supported shells (Bash, Zsh, Fish) "
"[`XDG_DATA_DIRS`](https://specifications.freedesktop.org/basedir-spec/"
"basedir-spec-latest.html#variables) is now populated with the path to the `/"
"share` subdirectory of the current profile. This means that command "
"completion scripts, `.desktop` files, and similar artifacts installed via "
"[`nix-env`](../command-ref/nix-env.md) or [`nix profile`](../command-ref/new-"
"cli/nix3-profile.md) (experimental) can be found by any program that follows "
"the [XDG Base Directory Specification](https://specifications.freedesktop."
"org/basedir-spec/basedir-spec-latest.html)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:77
msgid ""
"A new command `nix store add` has been added. It replaces `nix store add-"
"file` and `nix store add-path` which are now deprecated."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:79
msgid ""
"A new option [`always-allow-substitutes`](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-"
"always-allow-substitutes) has been added."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:81
msgid ""
"When set to `true`, Nix will always try to substitute a derivation, even if "
"it has the \\[`allowSubstitutes`\\]{#adv-attr-allowSubstitutes} attribute "
"set to `false`."
msgstr ""
